; qOS installer live-medium SELinux policy module (CIL).
; ===========================================================================
; Loaded ONLY on the installer live medium, at boot, by
; qos-installer-setup.service (which is gated on the `qos.installer` kernel
; cmdline). The INSTALLED system never loads this module.
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS
; ---------------
; The qos-installer UI runs under `cage` in the greetd session, whose SELinux
; domain is `xdm_t`. xdm_t is a login/desktop domain and is correctly denied
; the privileged container/install operations a whole-disk install needs.
;
; The privileged backend (qos-install) sidesteps this by re-launching its real
; work as a TRANSIENT systemd unit (`systemd-run`), so the dangerous operations
; (bootc image copy-to-storage, `podman run --privileged ... bootc install
; to-disk`, partition/mount of the freshly written disk) execute in a
; system-service domain (init_t) — which the base targeted policy already
; permits — and stay FULLY ENFORCED. See os/usr/libexec/qos-install.
;
; The ONLY remaining gap is that xdm_t must be allowed to ASK systemd to start
; that transient unit. This module grants exactly that, scoped to the ephemeral
; installer medium. It replaces the live medium's former global `enforcing=0`
; (os/installer-disk.toml): the whole system — including every privileged
; install operation — now runs enforcing; only the installer's UI/launcher
; session domain is relaxed.
;
; CURRENT POSTURE (reliable default): mark xdm_t permissive.
; -----------------------------------------------------------
; `typepermissive` makes the kernel LOG-but-ALLOW denials whose SOURCE domain
; is xdm_t, while every other domain (init_t, container_runtime_t, the install
; itself, the kernel) stays enforcing. This is chosen as the shipped default
; because the precise allow-rule set for "xdm_t may StartTransientUnit" cannot
; be finalised without capturing live AVCs on a VM install run (this build
; environment cannot boot the medium). It is a large, honest improvement over
; global enforcing=0 and carries no regression risk for the privileged path.
(typepermissive xdm_t)

; HARDENING PATH (tighten once a VM install run confirms the AVCs):
; ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Replace the `(typepermissive xdm_t)` line above with the narrow grants below
; (extend with whatever `audit2allow` reports from the VM run — see
; docs/selinux-installer.md). These let xdm_t reach the system manager over
; D-Bus and issue StartTransientUnit, without making the domain permissive.
;
; (allow xdm_t system_dbusd_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow system_dbusd_t xdm_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow xdm_t init_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow init_t xdm_t (dbus (send_msg)))
; (allow xdm_t init_t (system (start status stop reload)))
